--- !u!114 &-4885714847185209037
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'Audio adds so much richness to a game experience!


      You''ll no doubt have noticed that the robot makes audible footsteps when it moves.


      The robot also has an <b>audio listener</b> attached to it, which works like ears. The audio listener makes it possible to experience <b>spatial audio</b>, where sounds come from particular sources in the scene.


      To really add a distinct feel to the scene, let''s add some background sound.'
